From 4edd6b30e8e0eff386674db429d2496e46f0c5af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Update usrsctp: restart T3-rtx on a new cumulative ack

usrsctp's express SACK path (sctp_express_handle_sack, the common case of a SACK without
gap blocks) never restarts the retransmission timer when the cumulative
ack advances, contrary to RFC 4960 6.3.2 R3. While data stays in flight
the timer therefore expires every 2 x RTO however promptly the peer
acknowledges, and resends whatever is older than srtt + 4 * rttvar. With
a peer that delays SACKs for lone packets, such as libwebrtc's dcSCTP,
that cuts cwnd to one MTU about once per 800 ms at a 400 ms minimum RTO.

Minecraft Bedrock clients (dcSCTP) connected to a libdatachannel server
saw throughput capped at a few MTU per RTT and multi-second backlogs once
the RTT exceeded the server's write interval (GeyserMC/Geyser#6854).

Points deps/usrsctp at a usrsctp branch carrying the fix (cec6ee89f40e09266680699e4695952cc656b55b).

Written with assistance from Claude Code.
---
 .gitmodules  | 2 +-
 deps/usrsctp | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.gitmodules b/.gitmodules
index 5a98380..139585d 100644
--- a/.gitmodules
+++ b/.gitmodules
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 	shallow = true
 [submodule "deps/usrsctp"]
 	path = deps/usrsctp
-	url = https://github.com/paullouisageneau/usrsctp.git
+	url = https://github.com/onebeastchris/usrsctp.git
 	shallow = true
 [submodule "deps/libjuice"]
 	path = deps/libjuice
diff --git a/deps/usrsctp b/deps/usrsctp
index fec583d..cec6ee8 160000
--- a/deps/usrsctp
+++ b/deps/usrsctp
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit fec583d54493f879d2ae44a743423bf8a04371ab
+Subproject commit cec6ee89f40e09266680699e4695952cc656b55b
-- 
